# DeployTool.action
#
# The ROS2-action form of problog_project's DeployTool BT node (see
# module/contracts/schema.yaml's own DeployTool entry). Lowers a tool
# that's ALREADY installed -- currently restricted to tool kind=plow
# only (see tool_action_node.py's own docstring) -- same start/halt
# shape as InstallTool.action, a genuine mirror image reusing the exact
# same fixed-Duration/coin-flip machinery.
#
# Server: amiga_ros2_planners' tool_action_node, which runs this for
# `tool`'s own configured Duration (this problem's own config.yaml,
# tool.deploy.duration_seconds.<kind>), resolving a success/failure coin
# flip (tool.deploy.success_probability) once the full Duration elapses,
# or halting early if an always-on safety cutoff trips (battery
# depleted / collision detected -- safety_monitor.py). On success,
# tool_action_node marks its own tracked tool as DEPLOYED -- see
# move_to_node.py's own note on how that changes a SUBSEQUENT MoveTo's
# speed (tool.equipped.<kind>.deployed_speed), and battery_sim_node's
# own note on how it changes moving_drain_rate
# (tool.equipped.<kind>.deployed_moving_drain_rate). Only takes the
# input needed to execute: no triggers/reason port, and the result
# reports only success/failure (see `status` below), not why.

# The tool INSTANCE id (e.g. "plow1") currently attached -- same id= an
# earlier InstallTool.action goal used. Its own kind must be plow.
string tool
---
# Result

# true iff the full Duration elapsed AND the coin flip succeeded --
# false for anything else (a failed coin flip, a safety cutoff, a
# cancel, a precondition failure).
bool status
---
# Feedback

# Wall-clock seconds elapsed since this action started.
float64 elapsed_s
